packages/open-bitcoin-rpc/src/context/mempool_recovery.rs|.expect("fresh startup authority remains available before publication")|The handle is created immediately above, has no other owner, and therefore cannot have a poisoned or superseded authority before startup recovery publishes it.
packages/open-bitcoin-consensus/src/chain_spec/genesis.rs|#[expect(|This is the Rust clippy::expect_used lint expectation attribute, not a panic call; it scopes the three closed genesis constructor invariants below.
packages/open-bitcoin-consensus/src/chain_spec/genesis.rs|.expect("pinned 77-byte coinbase script")|The zero-argument private constructor concatenates eight fixed bytes and the 69-byte pinned ASCII timestamp, totaling 77 bytes below ScriptBuf's 10000-byte maximum; no candidate data enters.
packages/open-bitcoin-consensus/src/chain_spec/genesis.rs|.expect("pinned 50 BTC reward")|The zero-argument private constructor supplies the fixed 5000000000 satoshi reward within Amount's inclusive 0 through 2100000000000000 range; no candidate value enters.
packages/open-bitcoin-consensus/src/chain_spec/genesis.rs|.expect("pinned 67-byte output script")|OUTPUT_SCRIPT is a compile-time 67-byte array below ScriptBuf's 10000-byte maximum, supplied only by the zero-argument private constructor; no candidate bytes enter.
packages/open-bitcoin-rpc/src/context/canonical_chain.rs|.expect("memory-only context has no durable migration boundary")|Accepted legacy explicit fixture-only fail-fast API: configuration, storage, network or fixture recovery errors may panic; ordinary and sealed canonical startup use fallible constructors. Use from_fixture_runtime_config_with_store for fallible fixture preparation.
